# Public repo: the code, the design docs and the case-study site. What stays on this machine:
#   - third-party data: MetaTFT and lolchess (their terms: private use only), tftips / Blitz-derived catalogs
#   - Riot's art and match data, recordings and game screenshots (player names)
#   - research notes quoting third-party guides, and every model fitted partly on the data above
#   - keys and local tool state
# Allowlist for data/: only the game rules and the Set 19 roster (game facts).
/data/*
!/data/constants.json
!/data/manual/
/data/manual/*
!/data/manual/TFTSet19.json

/recordings/
/reports/
/research_notes/
/docs/knowledge/
/tests/fixtures/

# third-party content readers and the playbook (paraphrased third-party guides)
/tools/augment_archive.js
/tools/expert_letter_check.js
/tools/import_lolchess.py
/tools/build_playbook.py
/tools/playbook_review.py
/tests/test_playbook.py

# build outputs, local state, secrets
/capture/tftcap
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
*.pem
.vercel/
.claude/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mlmodel
.impeccable/
.playwright-mcp/
